  "source": "docs/findings/phys-02-baseline-state-rule.md, section \"Window test vectors\" (Phys, Sun 15 Nov): the seven cases of that table, with each history written out. The window is the last 14 mission days that hold a reading before the tested one (an earlier mission day, or the same day at an earlier time); a day counts once as the mean of its readings; median and spread (max(1.4826 x MAD, min_spread)) over those daily values; fewer than 3 days is no_data; a value more than 3 spreads from the median is outside_range. Every reading is in one context and no attention row applies.",
  "notes": "`spread` is rounded to 4 decimals; compare with the unrounded value. In 'the tested reading left out' the history holds the tested reading itself (day 15, 07:30); it must not enter its own window.",
